vault-shelf*.html
*.bak
demo-*.mp4
*.stackdump
# Any generated fixture, not just the default name: --out picks the directory and the
# generator is the artefact, so none of them belongs in a commit. The names of the three
# fixtures that decisions/0012 replaced are still ignored, so a stale one left in a checkout
# from before the change cannot arrive in a diff.
vault/
library-vault*/
sparse-vault*/
# The shared fixture store -- generated vaults keyed by generator digest, one copy for every
# worktree, self-invalidating. Never committed for the same reason the fixtures above never
# were: the generator is the artefact.
.fixtures/
dist/

# The generated vault -- a declared structure, not a mirror of anyone's notes. Regenerate
# with scripts/make-vault.mjs; never commit one, since the generator is the artefact.
demo-vault/

# The PII deny list itself. The whole point is that these names are not in a commit;
# .pii-names.example explains the file and carries no names.
.pii-names

node_modules/

# Built plugin artifacts. Obsidian gets these from the release, not from the repo;
# main.js is a bundle and would churn on every template edit.
/main.js
/styles.css

# A mirror of a REAL vault: same shape, invented words. Built by scripts/make-mirror-vault.mjs,
# a diagnostic you point at your own vault (design/0013, amended by decisions/0012). The
# generator is the artefact, and the thing it was built from is on somebody's disk rather than
# in this repository.
mirror-vault/

# The path to that real vault. No longer read by anything -- a mirror is `--mirror-of <path>`
# now -- and still ignored, because it is a vault path and that is exactly what check-pii
# refuses in a tracked file.
.mirror-source

# Agent worktrees. A worktree is a checkout, not a file of this repository.
.claude/worktrees/
